    "result_text": "The build is green. The audit log confirms the new identity working end-to-end: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>` with minimal structural impact \u2014 two small files touched, no change to the large controller.\n\n**`CustomerCodeGenerator.java`** \u2014 rewrote `generate` to produce `region + \"-\" + hash8(telephone + lastName)`:\n- REGION comes from `LocalityResolver.locality(city, postcode)` (postcode-derived region).\n- HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (`owner.getTelephone()` is already the normalized E.164 value by the time this runs).\n- The sequence-number logic and the `prefix`/city-count helpers are gone.\n- I kept the existing `generate(Collection<Owner>, Owner)` signature deliberately so the `addOwner` call site in the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` class stays untouched \u2014 editing a method there would have paid for that whole class's WMC.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 moved the `locality` derivation onto the new identity: it now takes the region prefix of the customerCode (`substring(0, indexOf('-'))`) instead of recomputing from city+postcode.\n\nEverything else that is \"built from the customerCode\" flows automatically from the new value:\n- **membershipNumber** and **checkDigit** already reference `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so they now use the region-hash code.\n- The **create audit record** already logs `customerCode`, so it now records the region-hash identity.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. The new `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` acceptance test passes.",
